SCRIP compiles them into its Prolog prelude through ../harness/scripts/util_gen_prolog_prelude_libs.py, which strips their comments
and blank lines, drops their module-system directives and hook clauses, and renames each library's unexported
predicates '$<library>_<name>' (SCRIP has no module system); the generated table is
src/parsers/prolog/prolog_prelude_libs.inc.  library(clpfd) (clpfd.pl, Copyright (C) 2007-2017 Markus Triska, the same
BSD 2-Clause terms) and library(csv) are embedded as SWI-Prolog itself compiles them: the generator runs SWI's own term and goal expansion
over the vendored file (../harness/scripts/util_gen_prolog_prelude_libs_expand.pl) and embeds the expanded clauses, because those
libraries define part of themselves through expansion (clpfd's cis/2 and parse tables, csv's library(record) accessors).  dcg_basics.pl is SWI-Prolog's library/dcg/basics.pl (module dcg_basics), vendored verbatim under its module's name.
